<h2>TWIA, flood insurance, and CRS</h2>
<p>San Patricio, Aransas, and Nueces counties are all in the TWIA designated catastrophe area. Many Aransas Pass owners therefore have separate policies for wind and hail (TWIA), for other perils (homeowners or commercial), and for flood (NFIP or private). TWIA covers wind and hail only, and TWIA claims generally must be filed within one year of the date of loss. For TWIA eligibility, work done on or after January 1, 1988, including re-roofs and roof repairs, needs a windstorm certificate of compliance. See <a href="/services/twia-windstorm-claims/">TWIA claim help</a> for details.</p>
<p>According to FEMA Community Status Book data (April 2025), Aransas Pass participates in the NFIP but not the Community Rating System. NFIP coverage generally starts 30 days after purchase, so flood coverage needs to be in place well before a storm. Homes near the levee and harbor should pay particular attention. Our article on <a href="/water-damage-vs-flood-damage-corpus-christi/">water damage vs. flood damage</a> explains why the cause of water matters so much to coverage.</p>
<p>Permit rules in Aransas Pass are set by the city; check with the city's building department before starting repairs.</p>

<h2>Common claim issues in Aransas Pass</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wind and water in the same home.</strong> Low-lying streets near the levee and harbor can see storm tide while the roof takes wind damage. TWIA pays for wind and hail; the flood policy pays for rising water. Each needs its own documentation.</li>
<li><strong>Manufactured homes.</strong> Damage to anchoring, tie-downs, skirting, and roofs is common after downbursts. Manufactured home policies differ from standard homeowners forms, so we read the specific policy.</li>
<li><strong>RVs and seasonal properties.</strong> RVs are often insured on separate RV or auto policies, and seasonal homes that sit empty may have vacancy conditions. Report damage promptly even if you are out of town.</li>
<li><strong>Salt air and metal.</strong> Metal roofs, carports, and fasteners corrode near the water. Insurers sometimes attribute storm damage to corrosion, so photos showing fresh tears, bends, and displaced panels help.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How we help</h2>
<p>We inspect the property, document wind, hail, and water damage separately where needed, and prepare an itemized estimate. For harbor and highway businesses, we also look at business income and equipment coverages. If you have already received a denial or a low offer, see our pages on <a href="/services/denied-insurance-claims/">denied claims</a> and <a href="/services/insurance-claim-supplements/">claim supplements</a>.</p>
<p>Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement. Corpus Christi Public Adjuster offers a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a> for Aransas Pass properties; you can also call or text [[phone]].</p>
